# November 20, 2026: Montgomery County, New York, west of Amsterdam (region mohawk, drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny). The Atlas had nothing in Canajoharie, Palatine Bridge, Fort Plain, Nelliston, Stone
# Arabia, Fonda's courthouse, Fultonville, Glen, Auriesville, Ames or Charleston's Baptist church. Standing places
# mostly: the 1770 Palatine Church, the two Stone Arabia churches, the Van Alstyne Homestead, the Arkell Museum and
# the Canajoharie district, the Frey house, Fort Plain's museum on the fort
# hill, the 1836 courthouse at Fonda, the Coliseum at Auriesville, the Fultonville, Glen and Nelliston districts, the
# Ames Academy and the First Baptist Church at Charleston; one ruin, the Otsquago Creek aqueduct walls at Fort Plain.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); HMdb marker pages, the Montgomery
# County historian's articles and contact page, fortplainmuseum.com, the Town of Minden page, Journal of the American
# Revolution, mohawkvalleymuseums.us, visitmontgomerycountyny.com, ourladyofmartyrsshrine.org (FAQ and calendar),
# OSV News (Trenton Monitor), WAMC and palam.org through tools/page.py. The Arkell Museum's own site
# reset every connection and was not read. National Register forms for these listings are not on NPGallery.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
